power: supply: sc27xx_fuel_gauge: UMP9620's saved capacity in Android's format, 100 % on the charger's Full

The FGU's always-on user area keeps the last capacity across a reboot. Unisoc's 5.4 driver (Android on the U30 Air)
keeps it as whole percent in bits 7:0 and tenths in bits 11:8 (sc27xx_fgu_save_last_cap()/read_last_cap() there):
the 575 (0x23f) that the first mainline boot with a charger driver read as 575 % is 63.2 %, with Android at 65 %.
The first version of this patch took it for 0.1 % (57.5 %) and wrote 0.1 % back, which Android reads wrongly
(580 = 0x244 = 68.2 %). On UMP9620 now:

- a saved value is read in Android's format, and written as whole percent (which is the same number in both
  formats). One that is no capacity in that format, or one that the first version may have written (a multiple of
  10 with tenths), is decided by the open-circuit voltage from the battery node's OCV table: right away with the
  battery at rest (under 50 mA); under load an ambiguous value is taken in Android's format
- the capacity is written to the user area whenever its whole percent changes, as Android does: mainline wrote it
  at a first power-on only, so every boot restarted from the value Android had left
- the charger's Full (from a charger driver, not 0006's guess from the current) sets the capacity to 100 % while
  the OCV table puts the battery at 70 % or more: the U30 Air's charger ends a charge at 4.208 V, below the top of
  the OCV table, so mainline's calibration (OCV above the table's top) never did. After a 1.5 h charge at 1.2 A the
  battery rested at 4.146 V with Full from bq256xx, and the capacity still said 58
- the reported capacity stays within 0-100: while charging nothing calibrates the coulomb count

--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
@@ -67,6 +67,19 @@
